{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607041500-etzhayyim-compat-catalog-to-kotoba-lang"
  :title "ADR-2607041500: etzhayyim *-compat catalog (1,027 repos) -> kotoba-lang, one repo per vendor, reverse-domain naming"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-04"
  :authoritative_for
  ["orgs/etzhayyim/root/20-actors/ holds 1,027 <vendor>-compat clean-room API-compat cljc actors (CRUD+pagination+filtering+validation over kotoba Datom log, generated from each vendor's public OpenAPI spec) - these are library-shaped code per ADR-2606302300's kotoba-lang admission rule, not etzhayyim public-interest organism actors, so they relocate to kotoba-lang following the kami-nv-compat precedent (ADR-2607020130)"
   "2026-07-04 scan finding: source is already ~2,055 .cljc files (no TS to port), but deps.edn is broken/vestigial in both observed shapes - pseudo-format {:dependencies {:kotoba \"workspace\" ...}} (not valid tools.deps) in the majority shape, or stale {:local/root \"../../40-engine/kotoba\"} (target dir no longer exists) in the older shape; actual test execution uses bb --classpath src:test(s) directly and never touches deps.edn, so the catalog already runs/passes with zero external deps despite the broken manifest"
   "naming rule: new_name = \"com-\" + kebab(strip-suffix(old_dir, \"-compat\")), ASCII-fold diacritics, underscores->hyphens; com- prefix chosen unconditionally (matches existing com-etzhayyim-*/com-junkawasaki convention) rather than per-vendor-accurate reverse-DNS TLD, which is out of scope for a 1,027-item mechanical pass"
   "per-repo recipe: copy to scratch -> replace deps.edn with valid self-contained tools.deps -> add README Provenance section -> git init+commit -> gh repo create kotoba-lang/<new> --public --source=. --push -> git clone into orgs/kotoba-lang/<new> -> add to manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects -> gen-west-manifest.bb --entry -> --check -> bb test green -> commit manifest to superproject main"
   "old etzhayyim/root/20-actors/<old>-compat/ directories are NOT deleted by this ADR; deletion is a separate follow-up PR once the full catalog has landed in kotoba-lang and in-tree non-consumption is reconfirmed at scale"
   "pilot batch (this ADR, 8/1,027 landed): nvidia_isaac-compat->com-nvidia-isaac, nvidia_cosmos-compat->com-nvidia-cosmos, nvidia_drive-compat->com-nvidia-drive, nvidia_nvml-compat->com-nvidia-nvml, adyen-compat->com-adyen, stripe-compat->com-stripe, anthropic-compat->com-anthropic, sentry-compat->com-sentry"
   "remaining ~1,019 repos: scoped and scheduled here, NOT executed by this ADR; rollout is batched ~25-50 repos/session, alphabetical by old dir name, progress ledger = manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects entries themselves (no separate tracking file)"
   "open question (undecided): whether kotoba-lang should really grow to ~1,027 repos vs collapsing some into multi-vendor repos - decided to proceed with the established one-repo-per-lib pattern for consistency (ipfs/pqh/kami-nv-compat/etc.), revisit if repo-count overhead becomes a real problem"]
  :related
  ["ADR-2606302300 (org taxonomy; kotoba-lang library-placement rule this migration follows)"
   "ADR-2607020130 (kami-nv-compat relocation precedent; NOTE that facade is a distinct, larger NVIDIA-Omniverse/Isaac-Sim engine-mirror project and does not overlap with the 4 nvidia_*-compat schema-CRUD actors in this catalog)"
   "ADR-2607012200 (umbrella kotoba-lang TS->CLJC refactor; different, smaller scope - the 8 etzhayyim-sdk facades, not this 1,027-repo catalog)"
   "ADR-2607022900 (pin-verification rule enforced by gen-west-manifest.bb --entry)"]
